WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:03.503 line:0%
♪♪

00:00:03.503 --> 00:00:07.640
-Hey, everybody. We just
wrapped up our final show

00:00:07.640 --> 00:00:13.279
of 2022, and in our staff
meeting today,

00:00:13.279 --> 00:00:14.480
one of our producers said,

00:00:14.480 --> 00:00:17.417
"You know, let's keep
in mind that

00:00:17.417 --> 00:00:18.551
as soon as the show is over,

00:00:18.551 --> 00:00:20.787
people are going to want
to get out of here.

00:00:20.787 --> 00:00:23.356
They have flights to catch,

00:00:23.356 --> 00:00:25.791
trains to catch, and

00:00:25.791 --> 00:00:28.794
traffic's pretty bad
with the tree.

00:00:28.794 --> 00:00:30.763
So.

00:00:30.763 --> 00:00:31.831
Let's keep it moving."

00:00:31.831 --> 00:00:36.402
[ Laughter ]

00:00:36.402 --> 00:00:40.206
But at the same time, it's just
so nice to be with each other.

00:00:40.206 --> 00:00:46.212
[ Laughter ]

00:00:46.212 --> 00:00:47.447
Last Thursday,
we showed a picture

00:00:47.447 --> 00:00:50.250
of what we called
a Nissan Maxima.

00:00:50.250 --> 00:00:53.219
We were told it was a photo
of a Nissan Altima.

00:00:53.219 --> 00:00:54.487
I wanted to be sure.

00:00:54.487 --> 00:00:59.859
So I went down to my
Nissan dealership.

00:00:59.859 --> 00:01:02.028
Get to the bottom of it.

00:01:02.028 --> 00:01:04.497
Long story short.

00:01:04.497 --> 00:01:06.566
I'm the proud owner of
a new Nissan Sentra.

00:01:06.566 --> 00:01:10.136
[ Laughter ]

00:01:12.171 --> 00:01:17.176
Showed a photo of Trump getting
shot out of a cannon.

00:01:17.176 --> 00:01:18.811
Some criticisms.

00:01:18.811 --> 00:01:24.183
One was that that tie is going
the wrong way.

00:01:24.183 --> 00:01:26.519
And another was he couldn't
fit into that cannon.

00:01:26.519 --> 00:01:27.687
[ Laughter ]

00:01:27.687 --> 00:01:29.689
I'm going to give you the tie.

00:01:29.689 --> 00:01:32.292
Can't defend it.

00:01:32.292 --> 00:01:35.061
But the way these cannons
work is you gotta

00:01:35.061 --> 00:01:37.797
jam something in there.

00:01:37.797 --> 00:01:39.933
It doesn't look like
it's going to fit.

00:01:42.001 --> 00:01:45.071
But you got to make it work.

00:01:45.071 --> 00:01:48.040
Sarah Jenks-Daly,
one of our producers,

00:01:48.040 --> 00:01:49.742
did the sweetest thing.

00:01:49.742 --> 00:01:54.080
She wrote
a holiday corrections poem.

00:01:54.080 --> 00:01:58.183
[ Laughter ]

00:01:58.183 --> 00:02:01.855
To the theme of "'Twas the Night
Before Christmas."

00:02:01.855 --> 00:02:06.759
And it mentions a lot of the
wonderful people I work with.

00:02:06.759 --> 00:02:08.561
[ Laughter ]

00:02:08.561 --> 00:02:11.197
Beautifully written.
Got choked up reading it.

00:02:13.533 --> 00:02:17.803
And the reason
I got choked up is

00:02:17.803 --> 00:02:21.040
Corrections does not accept
staff submissions.

00:02:21.040 --> 00:02:29.349
[ Laughter ]

00:02:34.220 --> 00:02:37.056
Told a long story last week
about trying to watch

00:02:37.056 --> 00:02:40.092
"A Charlie Brown Christmas"
on the plane

00:02:40.092 --> 00:02:42.461
and how we weren't allowed to
because someone on the flight

00:02:42.461 --> 00:02:44.697
was allergic to peanuts.

00:02:48.367 --> 00:02:51.704
It did not play in the room
because apparently

00:02:51.704 --> 00:02:54.507
everyone here
is allergic to jokes.

00:02:58.644 --> 00:03:00.045
I did make a mistake.

00:03:00.045 --> 00:03:05.518
I called the woman who worked
on the plane a stewardess,

00:03:05.518 --> 00:03:07.453
which is, of course,
an outdated term.

00:03:07.453 --> 00:03:08.620
I should've said
flight attendants.

00:03:08.620 --> 00:03:11.290
Apologies. In my defense,

00:03:11.290 --> 00:03:14.827
last Christmas we did
fly Pan Am.

00:03:14.827 --> 00:03:18.498
[ Laughter ]

00:03:20.499 --> 00:03:22.101
Also another correction
I'd like to make.

00:03:22.101 --> 00:03:24.670
I said the flight attendas--
Excuse me. I said the flight

00:03:24.670 --> 00:03:27.173
attendant told
us we couldn't watch

00:03:27.173 --> 00:03:30.142
"Charlie Brown Christmas,"
but I was paraphrasing.

00:03:30.142 --> 00:03:33.746
What she actually said was
wah-wah-wah-wah-wah-wah-wah.

00:03:33.746 --> 00:03:39.852
[ Laughter ]

00:03:43.590 --> 00:03:46.692
We talked about how much
Shoemaker likes

00:03:46.692 --> 00:03:51.030
the Grinch, but only before
he switched and how angry he is

00:03:51.030 --> 00:03:53.266
at the Grinch.

00:03:53.266 --> 00:03:55.701
And he's -- I mean,
especially this time of year

00:03:55.701 --> 00:03:57.736
because there's a lot
of Grinch decorations

00:03:57.736 --> 00:03:59.672
and they're all very triggering
for Shoemaker.

00:03:59.672 --> 00:04:03.175
And so he's always just sort of
bursting into my office

00:04:03.175 --> 00:04:06.812
to unload all his
Grinch anger at me.

00:04:06.812 --> 00:04:08.680
Saying stuff like, "I'll tell
you where that Christmas-loving

00:04:08.680 --> 00:04:11.284
wuss should never show
his face -- Shoeville!"

00:04:11.284 --> 00:04:14.554
[ Laughter ]

00:04:14.554 --> 00:04:21.694
But the thing about
Shoemaker, and again,

00:04:21.694 --> 00:04:23.796
he contains multitudes, right?

00:04:23.796 --> 00:04:25.331
A lot of times
he's really aggressive,

00:04:25.331 --> 00:04:27.300
ranting about how much
he hates Christmas.

00:04:27.300 --> 00:04:30.136
But then the other day
he wanted to talk to me,

00:04:30.136 --> 00:04:31.670
and I knew he wanted
to talk to me because

00:04:31.670 --> 00:04:33.539
he just starts
banging on the wall

00:04:33.539 --> 00:04:35.441
between our offices.

00:04:35.441 --> 00:04:37.343
Angry bangs, and I went in.
He goes,

00:04:37.343 --> 00:04:38.811
"Close the door behind you."

00:04:38.811 --> 00:04:40.246
And so I closed it behind me.
And then he just looks at me

00:04:40.246 --> 00:04:42.315
and goes,
"What's your Christmas dream?"

00:04:42.315 --> 00:04:45.718
[ Laughter ]

00:04:45.718 --> 00:04:49.221
I was like, "What?" He goes,
"What's your Christmas dream?

00:04:49.221 --> 00:04:52.090
If you could have one
Christmas dream come true."

00:04:52.090 --> 00:04:53.425
I was like, "I don't know.
I guess,

00:04:53.425 --> 00:04:58.531
you know, be with my family."
And then he's like...

00:04:58.531 --> 00:05:01.200
Which is his way of saying,
"Ask me what mine is." Right?

00:05:01.200 --> 00:05:03.535
So I'm like,
"What's your Christmas dream?"

00:05:03.535 --> 00:05:07.339
He goes, "That a Christmas angel
would change everything

00:05:07.339 --> 00:05:08.975
to chocolate.

00:05:11.377 --> 00:05:14.046
You hear a gliss

00:05:14.046 --> 00:05:17.250
and then everything in your life
would be chocolate."

00:05:19.452 --> 00:05:21.086
And I was, "Okay."

00:05:21.086 --> 00:05:23.156
And he's like, "If you don't
like it, get out!"

00:05:23.156 --> 00:05:27.493
[ Laughter ]

00:05:29.729 --> 00:05:32.265
We've been talking
about the time

00:05:32.265 --> 00:05:34.566
I wore the Mike Scollins
tank top.

00:05:34.566 --> 00:05:35.568
There's a photo there.

00:05:35.568 --> 00:05:40.973
[ Laughter ]

00:05:40.973 --> 00:05:45.777
And, you know, the picture --
That's T.J.

00:05:45.777 --> 00:05:48.214
Was a lovely artist who sent us
the picture of Scollins.

00:05:48.214 --> 00:05:51.583
And he sent a new one because
he noticed that in the photo,

00:05:51.583 --> 00:05:55.221
I'm holding a mike and that's
a Mike, Mike Scollins.

00:05:55.221 --> 00:05:58.724
And he did a beautiful piece
of new art that I think...

00:05:58.724 --> 00:06:04.497
[ Laughter ]

00:06:05.665 --> 00:06:08.901
We -- Scollins, who writes jokes
that make people unhappy.

00:06:08.901 --> 00:06:10.969
[ Laughter ]

00:06:10.969 --> 00:06:13.138
Wrote a joke about get
vaccinated because

00:06:13.138 --> 00:06:15.374
for no other reason
than Santa is 2,000 years old.

00:06:15.374 --> 00:06:17.309
We talked about this last year.
We showed a picture of Santa.

00:06:17.309 --> 00:06:18.478
A lot of people said that it
didn't look like

00:06:18.478 --> 00:06:21.213
2,000 years old, and then
we showed an older Santa

00:06:21.213 --> 00:06:23.516
and then Scollins, because I
think this would have --

00:06:23.516 --> 00:06:25.517
He sent me this. He goes, "I
think this would have made

00:06:25.517 --> 00:06:28.854
the get vaccinated because
Santa's 2,000 years old,

00:06:28.854 --> 00:06:31.190
I think this picture
would have made it work.

00:06:31.924 --> 00:06:40.199
[ Laughter ]

00:06:42.468 --> 00:06:44.804
In yesterday's "Closer Look,"
Sal made some jokes

00:06:44.804 --> 00:06:46.772
about weed dealers that Baze

00:06:46.772 --> 00:06:49.174
then busted him on, claiming
that anyone who thinks

00:06:49.174 --> 00:06:52.111
a weed dealer has things
like beaded curtains

00:06:52.111 --> 00:06:55.147
or a fanny pack clearly doesn't
smoke weed.

00:06:55.147 --> 00:06:56.849
Sal got very defensive.

00:06:56.849 --> 00:06:58.383
He told us all that
his weed dealer

00:06:58.383 --> 00:07:01.387
does, in fact, have a fanny
pack, and then to prove

00:07:01.387 --> 00:07:03.088
he has a weed dealer,
he took out a bag

00:07:03.088 --> 00:07:06.759
and opened it up,
and it was overwhelming,

00:07:06.759 --> 00:07:08.661
the odor of oregano.

00:07:08.661 --> 00:07:11.898
[ Laughter ]

00:07:15.334 --> 00:07:18.203
A lot of you noted that
Corrections has a lot of inside

00:07:18.203 --> 00:07:21.240
jokes about the crew
and the staff.

00:07:21.240 --> 00:07:23.108
Sarah's poem had a ton of them.

00:07:23.108 --> 00:07:26.512
Would probably play pretty hot
if I read it out loud.

00:07:26.512 --> 00:07:27.914
But rules are rules.

00:07:27.914 --> 00:07:30.382
[ Laughter ]

00:07:30.382 --> 00:07:33.119
So it's hard at times to know
what I'm talking about.

00:07:33.119 --> 00:07:34.754
So we thought
we'd give you a little

00:07:34.754 --> 00:07:37.657
primer on the new slang terms
we're using around the office...

00:07:37.657 --> 00:07:40.292
[ Laughter ]

00:07:40.292 --> 00:07:43.362
...in a segment called "Seth
Explains Late Night Slang."

00:07:43.362 --> 00:07:46.766 line:0%
♪♪

00:07:50.903 --> 00:07:56.008 line:0%
Our first and only new slang
term is "Baze of Glory."

00:07:57.542 --> 00:07:59.011 line:0%
Let's see the definition.

00:07:59.011 --> 00:08:00.646 line:0%
When you think
of something so funny

00:08:00.646 --> 00:08:02.114 line:0%
that you have to say
it out loud,

00:08:02.114 --> 00:08:04.584 line:0%
even though it works
against your own interests.

00:08:06.785 --> 00:08:08.888
Let me give you an example.
True story.

00:08:08.888 --> 00:08:10.957
Bass, our wonderful head writer,

00:08:10.957 --> 00:08:14.560
Alex Baze, got married
to Sue this year.

00:08:14.560 --> 00:08:15.961
His beautiful wife.

00:08:15.961 --> 00:08:18.263
Hadn't seen my mom in a while.
My mom comes to the show.

00:08:18.263 --> 00:08:21.900
Baze is talking to my mom and
Baze says to her,

00:08:21.900 --> 00:08:24.470
"I got married since
the last time you saw me."

00:08:24.470 --> 00:08:27.239
And then my mom says to Baze,
"How long?"

00:08:27.239 --> 00:08:29.641
Not "how long ago," which would
have made more sense.

00:08:29.641 --> 00:08:32.244
But she says, "How long?"
And because she said "how long,"

00:08:32.244 --> 00:08:35.548
Baze says to my mom,
"I give it two months."

00:08:35.548 --> 00:08:41.420
[ Laughter ]

00:08:41.420 --> 00:08:47.325
[ Laughter ]

00:08:47.325 --> 00:08:49.728
I should note Baze admitted to
us he then went home,

00:08:49.728 --> 00:08:51.597
right home and told Sue.

00:08:51.597 --> 00:08:53.799
Too good not even to tell Sue.

00:08:57.302 --> 00:09:00.072
We said Cheeto dust.

00:09:00.072 --> 00:09:03.308
Cheeto dust is called Cheetle.

00:09:03.308 --> 00:09:04.644
I didn't know that,
but that's the word.

00:09:04.644 --> 00:09:08.581
Also, Chester Cheetah
is the character's name.

00:09:08.581 --> 00:09:11.016
He was played by the actor
Don Cheadle.

00:09:11.016 --> 00:09:12.251
[ Gong sounds ]

00:09:12.251 --> 00:09:19.592
[ Laughter ]

00:09:19.592 --> 00:09:26.932
[ Laughter ]

00:09:26.932 --> 00:09:31.671
Speaking of mascots, I need to
put a stop to something.

00:09:33.439 --> 00:09:36.775
I have mentioned that
the most haunting mascot

00:09:36.775 --> 00:09:38.344
that I ever saw
on television was

00:09:38.344 --> 00:09:40.913
the McDonald's
character Mac Tonight.

00:09:40.913 --> 00:09:43.081
I was not joking around.

00:09:43.081 --> 00:09:45.083
And yet, because
we have given some of you

00:09:45.083 --> 00:09:47.052
a P.O. box address,

00:09:47.052 --> 00:09:50.889
you're taking advantage of that
and sending me

00:09:50.889 --> 00:09:53.159
things like this postcard.

00:09:54.060 --> 00:09:56.929
[ Laughter ]

00:09:56.929 --> 00:09:59.865
"We saw this and knew that,
as Mac Tonight's biggest fan,

00:09:59.865 --> 00:10:02.801
you had to have it.
With love, a couple of jackals."

00:10:02.801 --> 00:10:05.771
I don't want to see him.

00:10:05.771 --> 00:10:07.373
Ever.

00:10:07.373 --> 00:10:09.141
By the way, this, though, is
a dream

00:10:09.141 --> 00:10:10.376
compared to this nightmare.

00:10:10.376 --> 00:10:14.313
First of all, just addressed.

00:10:14.313 --> 00:10:15.848
From him.

00:10:15.848 --> 00:10:18.416
[ Laughter ]

00:10:18.416 --> 00:10:19.952
Black envelope.

00:10:19.952 --> 00:10:21.587
First thing I see --

00:10:21.587 --> 00:10:23.956
a $2 Mac Tonight phone card.

00:10:23.956 --> 00:10:25.824
[ Laughter ]

00:10:25.824 --> 00:10:27.893
Which I guess is what he, like,
tosses down to you

00:10:27.893 --> 00:10:29.829
when you're in his dungeon.

00:10:29.829 --> 00:10:33.665
[ Laughter ]

00:10:33.665 --> 00:10:35.368
And then this.

00:10:35.368 --> 00:10:36.969
Right?

00:10:36.969 --> 00:10:40.872
Mac with a picture.

00:10:40.872 --> 00:10:42.708
What the [bleep] is this?

00:10:42.708 --> 00:10:49.115
[ Laughter ]

00:10:49.115 --> 00:10:52.351
That's the mo--
I hate this so much.

00:10:54.486 --> 00:10:56.288
That's like a still
in a horror movie.

00:10:56.288 --> 00:10:58.657
And then a woman calls
the cops and the cops

00:10:58.657 --> 00:11:00.459
show up and he's gone.

00:11:00.459 --> 00:11:01.694
They're like,
"Tell us one more time

00:11:01.694 --> 00:11:03.028
what he looked like, ma'am."

00:11:03.028 --> 00:11:05.631
She's like, "It was --
It was a crescent moon."

00:11:05.631 --> 00:11:07.266
And then his partner's like,
"Waxing or waning?"

00:11:07.266 --> 00:11:08.300
It's like, "Not now, Mike."

00:11:08.300 --> 00:11:09.935
[ Laughter ]

00:11:09.935 --> 00:11:12.571
"I'm just saying,
if it was waning,

00:11:12.571 --> 00:11:13.639
might solve itself."

00:11:13.639 --> 00:11:18.043
[ Laughter ]

00:11:18.043 --> 00:11:21.446
Day drinking with Lizzo,
did it last Saturday.

00:11:21.446 --> 00:11:22.714
Aired it on Tuesday.

00:11:22.714 --> 00:11:26.318
Guys, lovely.

00:11:26.318 --> 00:11:29.688
My time with Lizzo,
may I never forget it.

00:11:29.688 --> 00:11:33.992
With that said, the fallout
of day drinking

00:11:33.992 --> 00:11:36.328
is always going home
to my family.

00:11:36.328 --> 00:11:38.129
And that night I'm just like,

00:11:38.129 --> 00:11:41.733
walking around,
you know, bumping into things.

00:11:41.733 --> 00:11:46.505
And my wife says from bed, "Can
you just please be careful?"

00:11:46.505 --> 00:11:49.374
And I say, "It's not my fault
that I'm out here

00:11:49.374 --> 00:11:51.910
getting loose.
Got to blame it --"

00:11:51.910 --> 00:11:53.279
And she says, "Stop."

00:11:53.279 --> 00:11:55.080
[ Laughter ]

00:11:55.080 --> 00:11:57.316
And I say, "Stop what?" She
goes, "I know what you're doing.

00:11:57.316 --> 00:11:59.919
You're quoting Lizzo lyrics,
and no one wants that from you.

00:12:02.521 --> 00:12:05.924
You're a 48-year-old man
with three kids."

00:12:05.924 --> 00:12:09.328
And I'm like,
"I'm being serious here.

00:12:09.328 --> 00:12:11.997
If you're mad at me,
you got to blame it on one,

00:12:11.997 --> 00:12:13.265
the Goose."

00:12:13.265 --> 00:12:14.567
[ Laughter ]

00:12:14.567 --> 00:12:16.902
"Two, my juice."

00:12:16.902 --> 00:12:19.371
[ Laughter ]

00:12:19.371 --> 00:12:21.273
And then she said, "Either
you're sleeping on the couch

00:12:21.273 --> 00:12:22.641
or I am."

00:12:22.641 --> 00:12:25.010
And I just said, "Ya-ya-yee."

00:12:25.010 --> 00:12:28.914
[ Laughter ]

00:12:28.914 --> 00:12:35.387
The next day, even worse because
now I'm just hungover, useless.

00:12:35.387 --> 00:12:37.622
Trying to be helpful,
trying to fight

00:12:37.622 --> 00:12:39.792
through my hangover.

00:12:39.792 --> 00:12:43.229
And one of our sons
had wet his bed.

00:12:43.229 --> 00:12:44.697
Totally natural.

00:12:44.697 --> 00:12:46.298
But I decided to be the
hero and I'm like,

00:12:46.298 --> 00:12:49.201
"I'm going to take care of it.
I'll strip the sheets."

00:12:49.201 --> 00:12:50.769
And I'm stripping the sheets.

00:12:50.769 --> 00:12:53.605
And there's one more sort of
like zipper sheet around it.

00:12:53.605 --> 00:12:55.775
And I yell downstairs, "Am I --
Which one?"

00:12:55.775 --> 00:12:57.976
And she goes,
"Anything that's wet,

00:12:57.976 --> 00:12:59.044
you've got to wash."

00:12:59.044 --> 00:13:01.012
Great. So I unzip that,
throw it in.

00:13:01.012 --> 00:13:02.781
Blah, blah, blah, wash it.

00:13:02.781 --> 00:13:07.286
And then the next day,
she's in -- I can tell --

00:13:07.286 --> 00:13:08.687
she's mad about something.
I'm like, "What's wrong?"

00:13:08.687 --> 00:13:11.924
She goes, "It took me --
You washed the wrong thing.

00:13:11.924 --> 00:13:15.127
It took me 12 hours to dry it.

00:13:15.127 --> 00:13:18.130
And I said,
"It took you 12 hours?

00:13:18.130 --> 00:13:20.966
Were you using a process called
doing it wrong?"

00:13:20.966 --> 00:13:24.169
-♪ Shot down in a ♪

00:13:24.169 --> 00:13:26.138
-♪ Baze ♪
-♪ Of glory ♪

00:13:26.138 --> 00:13:36.048
[ Laughter ]

00:13:40.519 --> 00:13:42.921
Alright.

00:13:42.921 --> 00:13:46.391
My assistant Chelsea brought me
this today.

00:13:46.391 --> 00:13:51.196
Bag. She said it was left
at the front desk.

00:13:51.196 --> 00:13:53.832
Of 30 Rock. Here's the postcard.

00:13:53.832 --> 00:13:54.966
"Happy holidays, Seth.

00:13:54.966 --> 00:13:57.402
For most enjoyment,
open during Corrections.

00:13:57.402 --> 00:13:59.371
Mikey the Shoe can take a peek
if you're unsure.

00:13:59.371 --> 00:14:00.605
Your secret jackal."

00:14:00.605 --> 00:14:02.608
Considered it all day

00:14:02.608 --> 00:14:05.744
whether or not I
should take a peek.

00:14:05.744 --> 00:14:07.045
Lot of effort was made, though.

00:14:07.045 --> 00:14:10.482
I did not show it
to Mikey the Shoe.

00:14:10.482 --> 00:14:11.650
That's the deal here.

00:14:17.822 --> 00:14:19.491
It's a [bleep] human head.

00:14:19.491 --> 00:14:25.164
[ Laughter ]

00:14:25.164 --> 00:14:30.836
[ Laughter ]

00:14:30.836 --> 00:14:32.004
It's worse.

00:14:32.004 --> 00:14:34.940
[ Laughter ]

00:14:45.751 --> 00:14:54.226
[ Laughter ]

00:14:58.764 --> 00:15:01.400
Um, I think that's all.

00:15:03.102 --> 00:15:04.703
I think that's about everything.

00:15:06.104 --> 00:15:11.043
[ Harp plays ]

00:15:12.778 --> 00:15:16.749
Was that the Christmas gliss?

00:15:21.853 --> 00:15:31.063
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:15:33.999 --> 00:15:35.634
Oh, one last thing.

00:15:37.869 --> 00:15:42.440
I referred to the Mario Bros.
character Bowser as a turtle.

00:15:42.440 --> 00:15:46.378
I was told Bowser
was not a turtle.

00:15:46.378 --> 00:15:49.414
He is, depending on who you ask,
a big sea dragon,

00:15:49.414 --> 00:15:51.716
a tortoise, or a Koopa.

00:15:51.716 --> 00:15:53.652
So Bowser is not a turtle,

00:15:53.652 --> 00:15:56.455
but I am an adult,
so I'm just going to move on.

00:15:56.455 --> 00:15:58.157
[ Clink ]

00:16:02.427 --> 00:16:05.898
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:16:09.201 --> 00:16:11.937
[ Laughter ]

00:16:17.643 --> 00:16:19.345
[ Laughter ]

00:16:24.283 --> 00:16:30.789
[ Laughter ]

00:16:30.789 --> 00:16:37.295
[ Laughter ]

00:16:37.295 --> 00:16:45.303
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:16:45.303 --> 00:16:46.572
Merry Christmas, everyone.

